WEBVTT

00:00.880 --> 00:06.560
With the aim of entering the Kalos League, Satoshi challenged the Eisetsu Gym to a Gym match for his final badge.

00:01.980 --> 00:11.860
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:07.150 --> 00:10.680
However, he was defeated by the Ice type Trainer Urup.

00:12.430 --> 00:17.640
Both of them burdened with their own doubts, Satoshi and Gekkouga disappeared into the forest.

00:18.660 --> 00:22.590
However, as a result their hearts went through a lot of growth,

00:23.150 --> 00:26.800
which allowed the two to finally make the power of Satoshi Gekkouga their own!

00:28.100 --> 00:32.870
With renewed resolve, Satoshi gets ready for the battle for his final badge.

00:36.590 --> 00:37.210
Satoshi...

00:39.720 --> 00:41.600
Don't worry. I won't feel at a loss any more.

00:42.350 --> 00:43.720
I'm seeing clearly.

00:44.260 --> 00:44.580
Yeah!

00:45.260 --> 00:48.180
Satoshi! Get your eighth badge, no matter what!

00:48.180 --> 00:48.520
I will.

00:50.120 --> 00:51.860
Excuse me, I request a Gym match.

00:52.820 --> 00:54.070
A rematch, right?

00:54.260 --> 00:55.500
We've been waiting for you.

01:02.200 --> 01:07.950
Satoshi Gekkouga VS Mega Yukinooh!
The Giant Water Shuriken Triggers!!

01:08.990 --> 01:18.880
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

01:08.990 --> 01:18.880
Z

01:17.070 --> 01:18.170
Glad you're here.

01:18.170 --> 01:19.300
This is one of those "return match" things, isn't it?

01:19.850 --> 01:20.300
Yes.

01:20.830 --> 01:21.320
So...

01:22.870 --> 01:23.840
So what happened after our last match?

01:28.950 --> 01:30.060
Was I worrying about nothing, maybe?

01:30.960 --> 01:33.060
Oh... You know. Forget about that question.

01:33.420 --> 01:35.120
Come on, let's get started already, shall we?

01:37.690 --> 01:39.180
It looks like it's going to be a good battle.

01:39.740 --> 01:42.490
Try to melt my ice with your fiery passion!

01:42.490 --> 01:43.280
Master!

01:43.820 --> 01:45.220
I haven't explained the rules yet...

01:45.600 --> 01:46.670
That's all right.

01:47.220 --> 01:49.060
He was here the other day too, so... you know.

01:49.540 --> 01:50.040
Right?

01:50.310 --> 01:52.540
Yes! I'd like us to get started.

01:53.550 --> 01:54.210
I know, right?

01:54.720 --> 01:57.250
But this is an official match, so...

01:57.250 --> 01:59.480
Let's not bother with minor details. It's just, you know...

01:59.920 --> 02:02.420
Whoever defeats three Pokémon wins.

02:02.970 --> 02:03.700
Easy, right?

02:04.230 --> 02:05.010
Uh-huh...

02:05.320 --> 02:06.750
How bold...

02:07.330 --> 02:09.510
He's so eager to battle, he just can't help it.

02:09.970 --> 02:10.930
That's that, so...

02:11.380 --> 02:12.210
Let's begin!

02:13.620 --> 02:14.750
Here goes!

02:22.470 --> 02:23.490
A Kachikohru, huh?

02:23.840 --> 02:25.180
This isn't what he did last time.

02:25.630 --> 02:27.820
I wonder what he is trying to set up with Kachikohru...

02:28.310 --> 02:29.150
We'll begin!

02:29.150 --> 02:30.860
Pikachu, you're up first!

02:32.840 --> 02:34.780
All right, begin the match!

02:38.680 --> 02:40.320
Let's go, Electro Ball!

02:46.220 --> 02:47.300
I knew it'd start to slide.

02:47.730 --> 02:48.840
Icy Wind!

02:50.650 --> 02:51.810
Pikachu, don't let your guard down!

03:01.440 --> 03:02.610
Charge in! Quick Attack!

03:08.860 --> 03:09.500
What happened?

03:10.030 --> 03:11.800
It is Icy Wind's secondary effect.

03:12.350 --> 03:13.790
Look closely at Pikachu.

03:15.660 --> 03:19.090
Because of Icy Wind, its body is starting to freeze, causing it to slow down.

03:20.670 --> 03:21.310
All right!

03:21.690 --> 03:23.270
Pikachu, Thunderbolt!

03:31.850 --> 03:33.890
It can still keep up with our speed, huh...?

03:34.430 --> 03:36.260
In that case, here's Kachikohru's trump card!

03:36.880 --> 03:37.380
Sharpen!

03:44.110 --> 03:44.750
"Sharpen"?

03:46.910 --> 03:47.630
What's that?

03:47.950 --> 03:49.060
It's so pointy!

03:49.310 --> 03:52.910
It is a move that raises its Attack power by sharpening its body.

03:53.830 --> 03:55.240
Add a Rapid Spin to that!

03:59.120 --> 03:59.750
Pikachu, evade it!

04:09.950 --> 04:10.340
Pikachu!

04:11.570 --> 04:14.120
On top of having its Speed decreased, it is now getting battered by these consecutive attacks.

04:14.950 --> 04:15.850
What now, Satoshi?

04:19.470 --> 04:19.990
I got it!

04:20.660 --> 04:22.310
Move, move! Keep moving around!

04:34.990 --> 04:36.110
Good job, Pikachu!

04:36.630 --> 04:37.080
Impossible!

04:37.580 --> 04:38.270
I see.

04:38.580 --> 04:39.560
What do you mean?

04:39.950 --> 04:43.000
By raising its body temperature, it was able to melt its frozen body.

04:43.610 --> 04:46.210
Satoshi and Pikachu turned their fiery passion into a counterattack!

04:47.470 --> 04:48.730
Well, isn't that interesting.

04:49.180 --> 04:50.410
Kachikohru, another...

04:51.120 --> 04:52.190
...Rapid Spin!

04:55.090 --> 04:56.180
Pikachu, Quick Attack!

05:00.920 --> 05:01.930
Iron Tail!

05:14.380 --> 05:15.160
Not bad.

05:15.680 --> 05:18.740
Kachikohru is unable to battle. Therefore, Pikachu wins!

05:20.130 --> 05:20.870
All right!

05:21.200 --> 05:22.330
They did it!

05:23.650 --> 05:24.880
Things are different from last time.

05:25.900 --> 05:26.720
He's back...

05:28.330 --> 05:29.580
The usual Satoshi.

05:31.160 --> 05:32.270
Return, Kachikohru.

05:34.720 --> 05:37.510
I've... You know. I've been waiting for this burning passion.

05:38.750 --> 05:40.200
Crebase, your turn!

05:48.980 --> 05:51.820
Fire me up a lot more, challenger!

05:52.290 --> 05:52.740
I will!

05:53.160 --> 05:54.980
And I'll win for sure!

05:57.290 --> 05:58.210
Let's go, Pikachu!

05:58.620 --> 05:59.740
Thunderbolt!

06:05.930 --> 06:07.290
Crebase, Avalanche!

06:16.760 --> 06:18.240
Pikachu, dodge by sliding!

06:20.740 --> 06:22.340
I expected you to do that.

06:23.210 --> 06:24.270
Gyro Ball!

06:28.610 --> 06:30.720
Pikachu, use Iron Tail on the field!

06:36.960 --> 06:37.360
All right.

06:37.810 --> 06:38.760
Stone Edge!

06:43.550 --> 06:44.700
Thunderbolt!

06:53.980 --> 06:54.720
Pikachu!

06:55.310 --> 06:58.690
Pikachu is unable to battle. Therefore, Crebase wins!

07:03.550 --> 07:05.480
You did your best, Pikachu.

07:09.290 --> 07:09.920
Come on,

07:10.500 --> 07:11.860
get me more fired up!

07:12.590 --> 07:14.870
So... You know. Who is your second?

07:17.290 --> 07:18.160
It's this guy!

07:18.560 --> 07:19.470
Go, Fiarrow!

07:25.110 --> 07:29.790
Interesting. They all have a gleam in their eyes.

07:30.320 --> 07:32.120
Let's go! Flame Charge!

07:39.090 --> 07:39.970
Stone Edge!

07:48.730 --> 07:50.520
What do you think? That hit the mark, right?

07:54.170 --> 07:56.150
Fiarrow, Steel Wing!

08:07.270 --> 08:08.250
It won't go down, huh?

08:08.820 --> 08:10.210
What power...

08:10.800 --> 08:11.500
Avalanche!

08:20.020 --> 08:21.700
Fiarrow, let your passion burn!

08:21.700 --> 08:22.760
Flame Charge!

08:34.510 --> 08:35.860
Brute force, huh?

08:38.270 --> 08:41.410
Crebase is unable to battle. Therefore, Fiarrow wins!

08:41.860 --> 08:43.190
You did it, Fiarrow!

08:48.200 --> 08:49.750
Now Satoshi has two victories!

08:50.250 --> 08:52.010
Yeah! This time they'll win.

08:52.230 --> 08:54.040
But they cannot let their guard down yet.

08:54.830 --> 08:56.110
Return, Crebase.

08:57.780 --> 09:01.450
How far you can go depends on how much you believe in your Pokémon.

09:01.450 --> 09:01.840
Yeah,

09:02.270 --> 09:03.710
I'm sure I believe in them.

09:04.870 --> 09:06.310
I want to know a lot more about you.

09:07.200 --> 09:08.710
This is my last one!

09:09.230 --> 09:10.390
Yukinooh!

09:22.000 --> 09:23.470
Yukinooh is last, huh?

09:24.330 --> 09:26.300
All right, show me more of yourself!

09:26.590 --> 09:28.510
All right. Let's do this, Fiarrow!

09:28.750 --> 09:29.900
Steel Wing!

09:33.900 --> 09:34.540
Wood Hammer!

09:40.290 --> 09:40.760
What?!

09:41.550 --> 09:42.910
You want to win against me, right?

09:43.420 --> 09:45.280
The match has only just begin!

09:45.670 --> 09:46.880
Fiarrow, Flame Charge!

09:49.740 --> 09:50.730
Ice Shard!

09:57.810 --> 09:58.830
Wood Hammer!

10:01.540 --> 10:02.400
Fiarrow!

10:08.870 --> 10:10.080
Fiarrow is unable to battle!

10:10.400 --> 10:11.910
Therefore, Yukinooh wins!

10:14.900 --> 10:18.880
Yukinooh had no trouble keeping up with Fiarrow's speed at all.

10:19.360 --> 10:21.920
It used Ice Shard to skillfully block any escape routes.

10:22.300 --> 10:22.690
What?

10:24.180 --> 10:26.190
This is what Urup-san is like when he is playing for keeps.

10:28.040 --> 10:31.200
You did your best. I won't let this be a waste, no matter what.

10:33.380 --> 10:34.890
I'm down to my last one too.

10:36.550 --> 10:38.520
Let's show them our power!

10:38.960 --> 10:40.500
Gekkouga, I choose you!

10:44.150 --> 10:46.780
Oh, there you are. I've been waiting for you.

10:47.410 --> 10:49.650
Let's go, Gekkouga! Aerial Ace!

10:55.950 --> 10:56.950
Water Shuriken!

11:05.730 --> 11:06.630
Energy Ball!

11:09.020 --> 11:09.730
Use Cut!

11:18.910 --> 11:19.860
Wood Hammer!

11:27.000 --> 11:27.580
Go on the defensive!

11:47.240 --> 11:49.340
Let's do this together, Gekkouga!

12:02.480 --> 12:03.400
Pokémon Quiz.

12:03.800 --> 12:04.820
The answer is...?

12:06.960 --> 12:16.970
Coming up next:

12:06.960 --> 12:11.930
Satoshi Gekkouga enters the fight!

12:07.940 --> 12:12.650
Pocket Monsters XY&Z is brought to you by these sponsors.

12:11.960 --> 12:16.970
Standing in its path is Mega Yukinooh!!

12:37.590 --> 12:39.800
There's the super-sized Water Shuriken!

12:40.240 --> 12:41.190
Yeah!

12:41.630 --> 12:42.520
Satoshi and Gekkouga's...

12:43.030 --> 12:43.930
...greatness!

12:44.240 --> 12:46.320
Go, Satoshi Gekkouga!

12:53.000 --> 12:53.870
Such burning passion...

12:54.430 --> 12:57.570
We're going to become much, much, much stronger.

12:58.160 --> 12:58.840
Nice.

12:59.920 --> 13:02.560
Show me this future of yours or whatever it is.

13:04.810 --> 13:05.800
Aerial Ace!

13:15.450 --> 13:16.130
Wood Hammer!

13:19.240 --> 13:20.030
Cut!

13:38.270 --> 13:41.310
Wow, it's like a completely different Pokémon from before.

13:43.210 --> 13:44.190
Water Shuriken!

13:54.770 --> 13:59.470
Just what made you two so strong within these few days?

14:00.190 --> 14:01.960
I get stronger <i>together</i> with my Pokémon.

14:02.260 --> 14:03.970
That's my way of doing things.

14:04.380 --> 14:05.240
Seems that way.

14:05.640 --> 14:07.480
This battle makes me feel that.

14:08.120 --> 14:11.120
Gekkouga became stronger for me.

14:11.810 --> 14:15.220
This is our first battle as our new selves.

14:15.910 --> 14:17.520
I could clearly see...

14:18.510 --> 14:19.680
...your true essence,

14:20.160 --> 14:20.630
your passion...

14:21.110 --> 14:22.030
...and your future.

14:22.590 --> 14:24.800
We have to... You know. Reward you accordingly.

14:28.470 --> 14:29.100
A Key Stone?!

14:29.660 --> 14:32.030
Bare your fangs, o freezing power!

14:32.590 --> 14:33.760
Mega evolve!

14:44.340 --> 14:45.180
A Mega Evolution!

14:45.530 --> 14:46.600
Mega Yukinooh, huh?

14:47.200 --> 14:50.320
You've got my soul so fired up...

14:50.930 --> 14:54.390
...so it's only polite to accept your challenge with a Mega Evolution.

14:56.640 --> 14:57.910
Let's give it all we've got!

14:58.250 --> 14:59.320
Water Shuriken!

15:00.760 --> 15:01.800
Ice Punch!

15:09.130 --> 15:09.840
It froze...

15:10.420 --> 15:11.230
...in no time.

15:11.540 --> 15:13.940
Mega evolving has increased its power dramatically.

15:14.700 --> 15:15.330
Don't worry.

15:15.870 --> 15:17.760
I'm sure Satoshi and Gekkouga will...

15:18.490 --> 15:19.390
Ice Shard!

15:24.110 --> 15:24.760
Dodge!

15:31.350 --> 15:33.060
Gekkouga, Double Team!

15:38.120 --> 15:39.300
Aerial Ace!

15:43.400 --> 15:44.140
Wood Hammer!

15:56.910 --> 15:57.450
It's strong.

15:58.550 --> 15:59.360
Ice Shard!

16:04.190 --> 16:05.710
Use Cut, Gekkouga!

16:11.540 --> 16:12.200
Oh!

16:14.360 --> 16:15.730
Go!

16:16.670 --> 16:17.410
Ice Punch!

16:28.500 --> 16:29.590
Keep coming at us!

16:30.770 --> 16:31.670
If that's how they want to play...

16:31.930 --> 16:32.790
Wood Hammer!

16:35.590 --> 16:36.780
Jump onto the frozen blades!

16:43.080 --> 16:44.090
Awesome!

16:44.090 --> 16:45.070
I had no idea you could use them like that!

16:48.320 --> 16:48.840
What?!

16:49.070 --> 16:49.850
Whoa!

16:50.270 --> 16:51.110
Ice Shard!

17:03.810 --> 17:05.010
Water Shuriken!

17:06.540 --> 17:07.390
Ice Punch!

17:13.170 --> 17:14.400
Aerial Ace!

17:26.740 --> 17:27.740
They went and...

17:28.340 --> 17:29.470
...broke my ice.

17:36.190 --> 17:38.970
Yukinooh is unable to battle. Gekkouga wins!

17:39.810 --> 17:41.240
Therefore, the winner of this match...

17:41.790 --> 17:44.530
...is the challenger, Satoshi!

17:45.310 --> 17:46.530
All right!

17:48.820 --> 17:50.330
All right!

18:02.600 --> 18:04.000
Congrats, Satoshi!

18:06.100 --> 18:07.640
You did it, Satoshi!

18:07.970 --> 18:09.460
Now you have eight.

18:09.460 --> 18:09.790
Yeah.

18:10.350 --> 18:11.350
Thank you.

18:13.600 --> 18:14.270
Welcome back,

18:15.210 --> 18:16.650
you who I admire.

18:26.600 --> 18:29.490
Wow, that was a heated battle.

18:29.790 --> 18:30.190
It was.

18:30.670 --> 18:33.180
Your... You know. Satoshi Gekkouga was strong.

18:33.760 --> 18:35.180
You've showed me something special.

18:36.300 --> 18:38.620
I can rest assured that this will be in good hands.

18:41.550 --> 18:46.190
Come on, take this. It's the... You know. The Iceberg Badge of the Eisetsu Gym.

18:49.310 --> 18:50.470
Thank you very much.

18:51.350 --> 18:54.260
I got the Iceberg Badge!

19:01.960 --> 19:02.620
Whoa!

19:02.960 --> 19:05.020
They look awesome when they're all lined up like this.

19:05.480 --> 19:07.750
Somehow this makes me deeply moved as well.

19:09.490 --> 19:13.120
You've... You know. You've got all your Gym badges now, right?

19:13.760 --> 19:16.180
So... You know. You can enter the Kalos League.

19:16.690 --> 19:17.130
Yes.

19:19.690 --> 19:24.440
Your Pokémon like you and I've now seen how much you believe in them.

19:24.890 --> 19:28.250
So... You know. I like you now too.

19:29.100 --> 19:31.510
Go and see with your own eyes how far you can get.

19:32.070 --> 19:32.340
I will!

19:48.720 --> 19:50.220
Thank you, everyone.

19:50.910 --> 19:51.820
But this is where things get serious.

19:54.810 --> 19:57.310
Lots of strong people will gather at the Kalos League.

19:58.060 --> 19:58.990
Shota will be waiting there too.

20:01.850 --> 20:02.290
Yeah.

20:02.770 --> 20:05.900
Together with you guys, I'll make a dash towards league victory!

20:08.130 --> 20:13.220
Satoshi has conquered the Gyms of the Kalos region and finally won his eighth badge.

20:14.140 --> 20:16.970
It's time to aim for Miare City,

20:17.670 --> 20:20.740
towards the Kalos League, where his rivals will be waiting!

20:28.780 --> 20:30.970
PokéLove TV!

20:31.530 --> 20:32.830
The hosts are I, Ken, and...

20:32.830 --> 20:34.590
Hi! I'm Jenny, nice to meet you!

20:34.590 --> 20:36.860
Today we will introduce Yukinooh!

20:36.860 --> 20:38.350
Its body is snow white!

20:38.350 --> 20:44.680
That's right. Yukinooh is called the Frost Tree Pokémon and is pure white so that it can hide its body in the snow.

20:44.880 --> 20:50.670
Not only that, but it's an amazing Pokémon that can make it snow with its Ability Snow Warning!

20:50.670 --> 20:52.870
Whoa, Yukinooh is awesome!

20:53.160 --> 20:54.210
All right, I've decided!

20:54.210 --> 20:55.070
Decided what?

20:55.070 --> 20:58.700
I'll catch lots of them, create a ski slope with the snow it makes fall, and make a killing!

20:58.800 --> 21:00.880
Don't use them to make money!

21:01.480 --> 21:02.490
How about this, then?

21:03.090 --> 21:04.580
This feels nice, doesn't it?

21:04.580 --> 21:05.070
It does.

21:07.710 --> 21:09.290
Now we are having a snowgazing bath!

21:09.720 --> 21:11.910
This is very exquisite.

21:16.560 --> 21:19.330
No, Yukinooh. That's too much.

21:21.040 --> 21:26.050
Sunday June 5th at 8am!

21:21.880 --> 21:23.840
Abareru-kun's automaton ends up...!

21:24.110 --> 21:25.120
On Sunday at 8am!

21:28.210 --> 21:30.120
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:30.320 --> 21:31.440
Towards our next adventure!

21:33.700 --> 21:35.500
I wonder if Numelgon's doing all right.

21:37.160 --> 21:38.810
Dedenne, you're really excited too, right?

21:39.650 --> 21:40.620
Look at that!

21:42.100 --> 21:42.970
A Melecie!

21:43.440 --> 21:45.620
Why are you doing this?!

21:46.360 --> 21:48.750
Next time on Pocket Monsters XY&Z:

21:49.230 --> 21:52.140
Find Melecie! Numelgon and Dedenne!!

21:52.450 --> 21:55.940
Next Time

21:52.450 --> 21:55.940
Find Melecie!
Numelgon and Dedenne!!

21:53.020 --> 21:54.170
Everyone...

21:54.170 --> 21:54.990
...keep Pokémon!

21:55.980 --> 22:06.030
Next episode:

21:55.980 --> 22:01.430
A Melecie is on a big rampage!?

21:56.870 --> 22:01.440
Pocket Monsters XY&Z was brought to you by these sponsors.

22:01.660 --> 22:06.030
How did this happen?
